{
  "title": "React 8: You Might Not Need an Effect",
  "subtitle": "React Explained",
  "audio": null,
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "Effects are an escape hatch.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "badge": "ASK: DO I REALLY NEED THIS?",
      "items": [
        [
          "Effects: sync with outside systems",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "Most bugs come from overusing them",
          "red"
        ],
        [
          "Prefer render and event handlers",
          "green"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "Effects are an escape hatch, meant for syncing with things outside React. Most effect bugs come from using them for things that need no effect at all, so ask first: do I really need this?",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/intro.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "derive",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 11.5,
      "text": "Derive values during render.",
      "visual": "compare",
      "left": {
        "title": "Effect + state",
        "color": "red",
        "items": [
          "Effect sets fullName",
          "Extra render, flicker"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "In render",
        "color": "green",
        "items": [
          "const full = first + last",
          "No effect, no extra render"
        ]
      },
      "say": "If a value can be calculated from props or state, calculate it during render. Copying it into state with an effect adds an extra render, and a moment where the screen shows stale data.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/derive.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "events",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 10.5,
      "text": "User actions belong in handlers.",
      "visual": "compare",
      "left": {
        "title": "Effect",
        "color": "red",
        "items": [
          "Watch a flag in state",
          "then post the form"
        ]
      },
      "right": {
        "title": "Handler",
        "color": "green",
        "items": [
          "Submit handler posts",
          "right when it happens"
        ]
      },
      "say": "If something happens because the user did something, do it in the event handler. Setting a flag and watching it in an effect makes the logic indirect, and easy to break.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/events.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "reset",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 10.5,
      "text": "Reset state with a key.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "// state resets when userId changes",
          "muted"
        ],
        [
          "<Profile",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "  userId={userId}",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  key={userId}",
          "pink"
        ],
        [
          "/>",
          "blue"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "To reset a component's state when a prop changes, don't write an effect. Give the component a key based on that prop. A new key makes React start with a fresh component.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/reset.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "memo",
      "min": 8,
      "duration": 12.5,
      "text": "Slow calculation? Memoize it.",
      "visual": "code",
      "items": [
        [
          "const visible = useMemo(",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "  () => filterTodos(todos, filter),",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "  [todos, filter]",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          ");",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "// only if it is measurably slow",
          "muted"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "For an expensive calculation, cache it with use Memo, which recomputes only when its inputs change. Don't reach for it by default. Measure first, since most calculations are fast.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/memo.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "needed",
      "min": 9,
      "duration": 13.0,
      "text": "When you do need an effect.",
      "visual": "chips",
      "items": [
        [
          "Subscribe to a store or socket",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "Control a non-React widget",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "Log analytics when shown",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "Fetch data (or use a library)",
          "pink"
        ]
      ],
      "say": "You do need effects to subscribe to an external store or socket, to control a non-React widget, to log analytics when a component appears, and to fetch data, though a data library often does that better.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/needed.wav"
    },
    {
      "id": "close",
      "min": 4,
      "duration": 4,
      "text": "Next: refs and the DOM.",
      "say": "Next up, refs and the DOM. Follow for more React.",
      "voice": "/audio/react-08-no-effect/close.wav"
    }
  ]
}
